{"content":[{"c":["ZIPH (P",{"c":["lace"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. One of the cities in the extreme south assigned to Judah’s tribe for an inheritance (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.24","r":"Josh.15.24","rawR":"Josh.15.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.24","value":"Josh.15.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 15:24"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. One of the cities in the hill country belonging to Judah’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.55","r":"Josh.15.55","rawR":"Josh.15.55","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.55","value":"Josh.15.55"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 15:55"},"), mentioned with Maon, Carmel, Jezreel, and most prominently with Hebron (cf. ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.42","r":"1Chr.2.42","rawR":"1Chr.2.42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.42","value":"1Chr.2.42"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:42"},"). Ziph has been identified with a site three miles (4.8 kilometers) south of Hebron. The surrounding wilderness region is probably the “wilderness of Ziph” where David hid from Saul (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.23.14-15","r":"1Sam.23.14-15","rawR":"1Sam.23.14-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.23.14-15","value":"1Sam.23.14-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 23:14-15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.26.2","r":"1Sam.26.2","rawR":"1Sam.26.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.26.2","value":"1Sam.26.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"26:2"},"). The Ziphites who betrayed David to Saul were residents of this city and the surrounding region (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.23.19","r":"1Sam.23.19","rawR":"1Sam.23.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.23.19","value":"1Sam.23.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 23:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.26.1","r":"1Sam.26.1","rawR":"1Sam.26.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.26.1","value":"1Sam.26.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"26:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.54.1","r":"Ps.54.1","rawR":"Ps.54.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.54.1","value":"Ps.54.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 54 title"},"). Ziph is later mentioned as one of the cities fortified by Rehoboam (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.11.8","r":"2Chr.11.8","rawR":"2Chr.11.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.11.8","value":"2Chr.11.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 11:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"ZiphPlace","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 15:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.24","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.24","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.24"},{"anchorText":"Jos 15:55","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.55","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.55","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.55"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:42","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.42","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.42","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.42"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 23:14-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.23.14-15","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.23.14-15","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.23.14-15"},{"anchorText":"26:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.26.2","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.26.2","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.26.2"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 23:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.23.19","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.23.19","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.23.19"},{"anchorText":"26:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.26.1","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.26.1","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.26.1"},{"anchorText":"Ps 54 title","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.54.1","rawQueryValue":"Ps.54.1","sourceRefExact":"Ps.54.1"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 11:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.11.8","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.11.8","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.11.8"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3975f6e70d91870fd8889b007a3ca25af01b2c3b1630d7